The program uses dynamic memory allocation for each line read from the file, which is freed after use. Error handling is implemented by logging processing errors to a separate log file, which is rotated when it exceeds 1 MB in size. The program also uses efficient data structures and minimizes memory usage for optimal performance.

The external dependencies include standard libraries for file operations and logging.']

