This code uses a semaphore to ensure that only one thread can access the shared data structure at a time. It also uses a mutex to protect the shared data structure from concurrent modifications by multiple threads. The `filter` function filters out any transactions that are older than 10 seconds, and updates the metrics accordingly. The `update_metrics` function logs any filtered transactions and updates the metrics. The `shutdown` function flushes any pending transactions and releases the semaphore and mutex. The `monitor` function monitors the function's performance and triggers alerts as necessary.

This code is a good example of how to use a semaphore and a mutex in a multi-threaded program. It also demonstrates how to use a shared data structure to store information that needs to be accessed by multiple threads.']

