The class integrates with an external video processing library for real-time filtering and edge detection, addressing challenges related to latency and resource contention. It considers the impact of computational load on system performance and designs the class to optimize throughput under varying conditions, including low-light and high-motion environments. Additionally, it accounts for hardware limitations and balances between power efficiency and performance, ensuring that the class can handle sustained high-definition video streams without significant degradation in quality.

The `VideoFrameQueue` class provides a simple and efficient way to manage a queue of video frames, while also providing the necessary functionality to support real-time processing and edge detection.']

