The `dicom_get_pixel_type` function retrieves the pixel data type of the image from the header, which can be one of the following:

* `DICOM_PIXEL_UINT8`: unsigned 8-bit integer
* `DICOM_PIXEL_UINT16`: unsigned 16-bit integer
* `DICOM_PIXEL_SINT16`: signed 16-bit integer
* `DICOM_PIXEL_FLOAT32`: floating-point number with single precision (32 bits)

The `dicom_get_image_width` and `dicom_get_image_height` functions retrieve the width and height of the image, respectively. The `dicom_get_compression_scheme` function retrieves the compression scheme used for the image, which can be one of the following:

* `DICOM_COMPRESSION_NONE`: no compression
* `DICOM_COMPRESSION_JPEG`: JPEG compression
* `DICOM_COMPRESSION_LOSSLESS_JPEG`: lossless JPEG compression
* `DICOM_COMPRESSION_RLE`: run-length encoding (RLE) compression

The function returns an error message if the pixel data type is not supported. The extracted information is returned in a struct with the following fields:

* `pixel_type`: the pixel data type of the image
* `width`: the width of the image
* `height`: the height of the image
