The function also checks if we have reached the maximum number of DNS queries per second using the `last_dns_query` variable, which stores the time of the last DNS query in seconds. If we have reached the maximum number of queries, it sets the `error` variable to a descriptive message and returns the resolved IP with the error.

The function logs relevant information if logging is enabled using the `write_to_file` function. It writes the log message to the specified file path, ensuring logs are not too verbose but capture essential details.']

