The function `resizeUEContextCache` handles dynamic cache resizing for the UE contexts by evicting the least recently used UE contexts when the new size is smaller than the current size, or allocating new memory for the new UE contexts when the new size is larger than the current size. The function also supports concurrent access and locking to prevent contention between threads.

The function `reconfigureNetworkSettings` handles dynamic reconfiguration of network settings for the UE contexts by invalidating existing UE contexts that no longer match the new network configuration parameters and rebuilding the linked list accordingly. The function also supports concurrent access and locking to prevent contention between threads.

The function `updateNetworkConfiguration` handles real-time updates of network configuration parameters for the UE contexts by updating the corresponding UE context with the new network configuration parameters. The function also supports concurrent access and locking to prevent contention between threads.

